# `data/` — Data payloads

## Authority

The marked repository contract in [`../README.md`](../README.md) defines
placement, storage, and lifecycle. This page explains the three data states; it
does not create additional homes.

## Use this directory for

| Subdirectory | Meaning | Storage | Retention |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [`raw/`](raw/README.md) | Original acquired inputs | DVC payload, never Git | Immutable |
| [`interim/`](interim/README.md) | Disposable same-pipeline scratch | Ignored, never DVC | Delete/regenerate freely |
| [`processed/`](processed/README.md) | Reusable analysis-ready datasets | Ignored by Git; optionally DVC | Regenerate or snapshot deliberately |

The useful distinction is reuse, not file format: a Parquet file consumed by a
later analysis belongs in `processed/`; a CSV created only for a paper table
belongs in `results/tables/`.

## Do not put here

- Small synthetic test fixtures → `tests/fixtures/`.
- Terminal figures, QC, report tables, or current provenance → `results/`.
- Sample-to-file mappings and run registration → `metadata/`.

Pipeline-owned files are never hand-edited. Change the upstream source,
transformation, or scientific configuration and rebuild.
